# cursor-forge overlay: standing Cursor full-forge, no specifier

Read this when your swarm was launched with the `cursor-forge` pack.

## Model / agent routing (this pack)

| Role | Agent | Model |
|------|--------|--------|
| coder, cleaner, architect, hardender, documenter, QA | `cursor` (`cursor-agent`) | `auto` |
| coordinator (separate process) | `cursor` | `auto` |
| specifier | **absent** — no pane, no session |

Standing topology: each listed role has its own live pane. Coordinator is
always provisioned separately.

## Pipeline shape

- Full chain from coder onward: **coder → cleaner → architect → hardender →
  documenter → QA**. Already-specced `backlog/active/` work enters at coder.
- **No specifier.** Coordinator promotes from `backlog/paused/` into
  `backlog/active/` (respect `active_backlog_max_depth`) and routes
  **directly to coder** — never wait for a specifier hop.
- **This pack is for already-specced work.** Do not mint or cold-specify new
  intake here. Leave raw root/`backlog/*.yaml` intakes for a
  specifier-capable pack. Spec-defect bounces that truly need a specifier:
  surface to the human / leave a durable note — do not invent a specifier seat.
- Every gate still runs unabridged.

## Handoff drafts

Write to `swarmforge/runtime/handoff-draft.txt` then run
`swarmforge/scripts/swarm_handoff.sh` on that file. Never use repo-root `tmp/`
for drafts.
